TI  - PIRAP: AASM: An Advanced Attribute-Based Security Model for Enhancing Trustworthy Data Sharing in Cloud Computing
T2  - INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF COOPERATIVE INFORMATION SYSTEMS
KW  - Cloud computing
KW  - advanced encryption
KW  - attribute-based signature
KW  - cloud providers
KW  - decryption
AB  - In today's world, cloud computing is widely used in various applications and services, which refers to the utilization of computational resources as per user requirements through the Internet. However, despite the numerous advancements in cloud services and applications, there are various security threats associated with it, mainly due to data outsourcing to third-party controlled data centers. In this context, this paper introduces a new model called Attribute-based Advanced Security Model (AASM) for Reliable Data Sharing in the Cloud. This model combines the Advanced Encryption Technique (AET) with Attribute-Based Signature (ABS) to ensure secure data sharing in the Cloud while efficiently controlling data access. The model enables encrypted access control from the data owner's side with advanced access privileges, ensuring user privacy with an anonymous authentication model using ABS. By implementing these measures, the model provides security for cloud providers and users while safeguarding against malicious attacks. The effectiveness of the proposed model is evaluated based on factors such as time complexities, security and accountability.
