TI  - SUBLμME: Secure Blockchain as a Service and Microservices-based Framework for IoT Environments
T2  - 2021 IEEE/ACS 18TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON COMPUTER SYSTEMS AND APPLICATIONS (AICCSA)
CP  - 18th ACS/IEEE International Conference on Computer Systems and Applications (AICCSA)
KW  - Internet of Things
KW  - Security
KW  - Microservices
KW  - Blockchain
KW  - BaaS
KW  - INTERNET
AB  - IoT applications have extended new concepts to smart technologies in different vital sectors such as healthcare, education, agriculture, energy management and control, etc. IoT aims to interconnect several intelligent devices over the Internet to control, store, exchange, and analyze collected data. However, the main problem in IoT environments is that they present numerous potential vulnerabilities that can be the origin of security attacks. In this context, this paper proposes a novel framework, named SUBL mu ME, which stands for SecUre BLockchain as a service and uservices-based fraMework for IoT Environments. This framework integrates BaaS and microservices technologies that have the predominant characteristic of offering reusable and reconfigurable security features implemented as independent services that can be reused for multiple IoT applications. SUBL mu ME is implemented and validated by a simulated smart home environment. The results of the simulation experiments showed that SUBL mu ME brings several security improvements in terms of performance, data integrity, data packages' validation, access control, and efficient and secure data transmission and storage.
