AB  - We propose a new access control mechanism for video surveillance system based on user's biometrics, which allows to access real-time video surveillance data from deployed Internet of Things (IoT) smart devices. For this purpose, mutual authentication is performed between a user and accessed smart devices via the cloud server(s) and the session keys are then established to make secure communication. The proposed scheme allows accessing real time video and older videos that are in cloud servers, and also user's credential update phase. Through the security analysis, it has been shown that the proposed scheme is robust against a variety of potential passive/active attacks. A detailed comparative study shows the efficacy of the proposed scheme as compared to other existing solutions. Finally, the real testbed experiments have been carried out for secure surveillance system using Raspberry PI devices as IoT devices, user's devices and servers to show its practical application.
