TI  - Enabling a Multi-Level Users Management Policy in Cloud of Big Data
T2  - PROCEEDINGS OF THE 2018 10TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON ELECTRONICS, COMPUTERS AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE (ECAI)
CP  - 10th International Conference on Electronics, Computers and Artificial Intelligence (ECAI)
KW  - cloud
KW  - big data
KW  - Policy
KW  - privacy
KW  - Access Control
AB  - In computing, one of the rapidly growing technologies is cloud computing, which comes with great benefits, as well as with some drawbacks. One of the issues examined in the present paper is the secure clients' location sharing method, from the perspective of data integrity and authenticity. These are issues associated with sharing of data in cloud-based locations. The first aspect to analyze is the access mechanism, which raises security issues if it is not secured enough for sensitive data. Data stored in cloud (big data) is often accessed by third party, which increases the exposure to attacks. The privacy violation risks thus become higher. Cloud-stored data usually is processed or used by third party. Data owners (clients) must ensure information privacy of the stored or processed data. The solution proposed in this paper for cloud data management and classification is a schema organized on multiple levels and based on policy in order to increase reliability of cloud computing in terms of confidentiality of sensitive data. The paper is based on a solid security policy structure which follow the specifications and abilities. The algorithm presented in the paper efficiently provides data accuracy and validity with the employment and management of the outlined policies, complying to cloud customers' specifications and cloud providers' possibilities.
