KW  - Clinical Information Processing
KW  - Special Health Services Registry (RES)
KW  - Privacy-as-a-Service Platform (PGaaS)
KW  - Open Web Application Security Project (OWASP)
KW  - Artificial Intelligence (IA)
KW  - Data Encryption
KW  - Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)
AB  - This study proposes a framework that leverages ML algorithms for the cybersecurity of telemedicine systems in the Department of Cordoba, Colombia, addressing challenges amplified by the COVID-19 pandemic. The framework emphasizes enhancing the processing capabilities and reliability in managing clinical information, particularly focusing on the RES. It integrates a PGaaS aligned with the OWASP guidelines, aiming to neutralize emerging threats using advanced IA models. The system incorporates data encryption, 2FA-based Access Control, continuous backups, code obfuscation, and watermarking, all supported by a suitable legal framework. These components are combined into a comprehensive monitoring and auditing scheme to ensure robust protection against intelligent intrusions and the compromise of medical data.
